  "body": "Found during the review of PR #1934 (fix for #1928). That PR adds seven new refusal and routing branches. Five have tests that name the refusal. Three do not:\n\n1. Side Auto on a part that changes sides between levels.\n2. The non-positive-offset guard.\n3. The shared fold refusal.\n\nA refusal without a name test can disappear in a later refactor. The code is correct today; the review confirmed it by reading.\n\nDone means: three tests, one for each item above. Each test names the refusal in its assert. The tests live in `crates/app/tests/` next to the other #1928 pins.\n\nRefs #1934 (partial; the fix itself is complete).\n",
